{title: 440 Quiero, Jesús, contigo andar}
{key: D}
{time: 3/4}
{lyricist: Washington Gladden, 1879 (1836-1918); Vers. esp.: Héctor Pereyra Suárez (1922-}
{composer: H. Percy Smith, 1874 (1825-1898)}

{sov}
1. [D]Quiero, [G]Jesús, con[D]tigo an[G]dar, [A]
y en tu [A7][D]servicio [E7]traba[A]jar;
[A7]dime el secreto [D]de [G]saber [Em]
[D][A]llevar [Bm]mis car[A]gas con [D][Em][A7][D]placer.
{eov}

{sov}
2. [D]Haz que mi [G]lengua [D]sepa ha[G]blar, [A]
solo el [A7][D]lenguaje [E7]del a[A]mor,
[A7]y al extraviado [D]pue[G]da gui[Em]ar
[D][A]hasta [Bm]el re[A]dil de [D][Em][A7][D]mi Pastor.
{eov}

{sov}
3. [D]Tenme a tu [G]lado, en[D]sé[G]ñame, [A]
a ser [A7][D]paciente, [E7]noble y [A]fiel;
[A7]que en tus pisadas [D]pue[G]da an[Em]dar,
[D][A]y al [Bm]aba[A]tido [D][Em][A7][D]consolar.
{eov}

{sov}
4. [D]Dame del [G]cielo [D]aquella [G]fe [A]
que en la [A7][D]tormenta [E7]ve la [A]luz.
[A7]Colme mi alma [D]tu [G]bon[Em]dad,
[D][A]y vi[Bm]va [A]siempre [D][Em][A7][D]con tu paz.
{eov}
